l. who have signed the DSU for benefits under the right to education after the deadline for submitting a scholarship application; m. for whom it has not been possible to obtain ISEE data within the time limits laid down in Article 11(8) of Prime Ministerial Decree 159/2013, and in particular applications that refer to certificates/DSUs:

• Not found in the INPS database; • Do not include the ISEE for university education grants and/or do not relate to the student applying for the benefits; • Not yet calculated for the purposes of determining ISEE values (certificate); n. who have submitted their application after the deadline set out in this call for applications;

o. who are either behind in their studies or repeating a year; p. foreign nationals who do not hold a residence permit for the academic year 2026/2027; q. students enrolled on the open semester referred to in Legislative Decree No.
